    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find where the expression is undefined, we set the denominator equal to zero: \\[\n\\frac{y+6}{y^2 - 5y + 4} = 0.\n\\]\n\nFor the fraction to be zero, the denominator must be zero: \\[\ny^2 - 5y + 4 = 0.\n\\]\n\nWe factor the quadratic using the $ac$ method. The product of the two roots must be 4 and their sums must be -5. So, the roots are $-1$ and $-4$: \\[\n-1 \\cdot -4 = 4 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad -1 + -4 = -5.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the quadratic factors as: $$\\begin{align*} -(y - -1)(y - -4) &= 0 \\\\ - (y + 1)(y - 4) &= 0. \\end{align*}$$\n\nSetting each bracketed factor equal to zero gives the 2 answers: \\[\n\\begin{align*} y + 1 &= 0 \\qquad \\text{or} \\qquad y - 4 = 0 \\\\ y &= -1 \\qquad \\text{or} \\qquad y &= 4. \\end{align*} $$\n\nThe sum of the values of $y$ in this case is \\boxed{-5}. The answer is: -5",
